The Organon, or Logical Treatises, of Aristotle (@greek-source-organon: 0, is #book, #part-of @greek-further-sources) { r_2EF6CZDKWTG5TQNGR0VQ3XXR9C
Aristotle; translated, with notes and an introduction, by Octavius Freire Owen. London: H. G. Bohn, 1853, two volumes, with Porphyry's introduction. English.

[Text or edition reference](https://catalogue.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/cb300275910). [Digitised volume I](https://archive.org/details/organonorlogicalt01aris). Use the contents to distinguish Aristotle's treatises from Porphyry's introductory text and Owen's notes. The two-volume catalogue identifies the edition for the further reading in volume II.

**Used passages:** Volume I: Categories, chapters 1–5; Prior Analytics I.1–4. Volume II: Posterior Analytics I.1–3 and I.13.

**Read with:** [The reading guide](../aristotle/Logic-and-demonstration.lingua#r_1SRR6TVQ8CC029F7QK6PKPM1X9). **Return:** [Further primary readings](Further-primary-readings.lingua#r_6JNQVRM8BSTH1VW99AFPR4G5QM) · [Ancient Greek philosophy](../Ancient-Greek-Philosophy.lingua#r_464ZHR7ZYC234A0XX2QEW47VB3).
